# This repo is checked out AS ~/.config/opencode — the directory opencode writes
# into at runtime, and the directory that holds any credentials. So it denies by
# default and allow-lists the configuration, rather than chasing generated files
# one by one. A deny-list goes stale every time opencode or a plugin starts
# writing something new; this one cannot.

/*

!/.gitignore
!/.github/
!/README.md
!/check.sh
!/AGENTS.md
!/opencode.json
!/skills/

# Never tracked, for the record — each is already covered by the deny above:
#   node_modules/            installed by opencode for @opencode-ai/plugin
#   package.json             written by opencode, not authored here
#   package-lock.json
#   bun.lock
#   auth.json               opencode's credential store
#   *.bak-*                  manual rollback copies
